<title>USA: Outdoor Systems completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Outdoor Systems completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Outdoor Systems Inc said on Monday it completed its $1.0 billion acquisition of Minnesota Mining and Manufacturing Co's (3M) outdoor advertising unit, National Advertising Co.</p>
<p>In a statement, Outdoor Systems said it now reaches 75 percent of the U.S. population with roughly 220,000 poster, bulletin, bus shelter, subway and mall displays in 46 states.</p>
<p>Outdoor Systems sold certain markets it acquired from 3M to Lamar Advertising Company for $116 million in cash.</p>
<p>Outdoor Systems also said it applied to list its stock on the New York Stock Exchange. It expects the shares to begin trading on the NYSE in September under the symbol OSI.</p>
